                <head>PM–1. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On May 2, 1958, Panamanian students entered the Panama Canal Zone and planted
                    Panamanian flags in front of the Administration Building and other predetermined
                    public places in Balboa in support of their “Operation Sovereignty” and urged
                    Ernesto de la Guardia, Jr., the President of Panama, to initiate negotiations
                    with the United States to have the Panamanian flag flown in the Canal Zone.
                    President de la Guardia, in an effort to appease student demands, sought the
                    advice of Panama’s National Council of Foreign Relations concerning the most
                    convenient approach to such negotiations. Representatives of the Republic of
                    Panama, however, did not initiate a request to negotiate. Documentation
                    concerning these events is in Department of State files 719.00 and
                    911F.7301.</p>
            </div>
